WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.550
Listen to this.

2
00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.750
«J'aime le sport.» «Je n'aime pas
le rugby.» Perfectly correct French.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.860
But it sounds like a robot
reading a shopping list.

4
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.490
Now try telling a whole story that way.

5
00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.950
Stop. Start. Stop.

6
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.840
Start. Your listener drifts off.

7
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.900
Fluent speakers sound different.

8
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.290
Their ideas flow into each other.

9
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.680
So how do you turn short,

10
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.310
choppy French sentences
into one that sounds fluent?

11
00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.010
In this mission, you'll
tell a story in order,

12
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.610
stone by stone.

13
00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:35.090
Then you'll rebuild pairs of sentences
to match the English in the lab.

14
00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.880
Your mission: build French that flows.
